    "summary": "Flowering-plant genus native to South and Central America, where it grows in forest openings and along riverbanks and goes dormant during the dry season. Several species are ornamentals with large, arrowhead-shaped leaves patterned in white, pink and red; all parts are poisonous.",
    "humanEdibility": "no",
    "edibilityNote": "All parts are poisonous and should not be ingested.",
